  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inter-Agency Working Group on Interoperability of Baseline Population, Displacement, and Refugee Data (IAWG-Interop.)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United Nations Population Fund (UNFPA) seeks to further expand the availability, quality and usability of Common Operational Dataset on Population Statistics (COD-PS) datasets around the world - particularly in operational response countries. Establishing and maintaining COD-PS datasets that are interoperable with displacement and refugee data and the broader set of humanitarian-focused datasets is fundamental for effective humanitarian response. 
 
UNFPA, in partnership with Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs, International Organization for Migration (IOM), Worldpop and UN High Commissioner for Refugee, is addressing the most pressing COD-PS challenges facing the international humanitarian system through this three-year program to advance baseline population data in humanitarian settings through data in humanitarian settings through improved data technology standards.</narrative>
  </description>
